      "message": "\u003e let\u0027s discuss whether the proposed tree makes sense.\n\nI\u0027m not following how the Trusty VM test instance gets installed and run on the Trusty VM from this CL, but I think it generally looks good to me. (maybe an answer to my other question in `rules.mk` will clarify)\n\n\u003e embedding the Trusty mock reference implementation under the default folder to make it more straightforward for OEMs to review and adopt.\n\n+1 - I like the example implementation of the service here, next to the service.\n\n\u003e proposing a android white-box fuzzing of the mock implementation\u0027s core logic\n\n+1 - fuzzing the implementation library with `fuzz_service` is the way to go.\n\n\n-------- \n\nI think my main question as a reviewer is: how do I know that this test will be run in a Trusty VM during VTS to check the partner\u0027s implementation in the TEE?\n\nIs that somewhere in the rules.mk, or something to do with `TRUSTY_RUST_USER_TESTS`?",
